) and three equivalent Se(2) atoms to form a mixture of corner and edge-sharing BiSe6 octahedra. The corner-sharing octahedra are not tilted. All Bi(1)-Se(1) bond lengths are 3.06 Å. All Bi(1)-Se(2) bond lengths are 2.86 Å. There are two inequivalent Se sites. In the first Se site, Se(1) is bonded to six equivalent Bi(1) atoms to form edge-sharing SeBi6 octahedra. In the second Se site, Se(2) is bonded in a distorted T-shaped geometry to three equivalent Bi(1) atoms.","dimensionality":2,"mineral":null,"mineral_distance":-1,"tool":"robocrystallographer","doi":"10.1557/mrc.2019.94"},"polyhedra":{"types":[{"type_id":"Bi1-Se6","center":"Bi","wyckoff":"6c","ligand_formula":"Se6","connectivity":{"corner":3.0,"edge":9.0},"n_instances":6,"cn":6,"shape":"octahedron","avg_bond":2.956903,"volume":34.335045,"distortion":0.033839,"econ":5.726744,"qe":1.00378,"bav":9.24933,"bvs":3.040206},{"type_id":"Se1-Bi6","center":"Se","wyckoff":"3a","ligand_formula":"Bi6","connectivity":{"edge":6.0},"n_instances":3,"cn":6,"shape":"octahedron","avg_bond":3.056979,"volume":37.68203,"distortion":0.0,"econ":6.0,"qe":1.007213,"bav":27.095177,"bvs":2.23742}],"sites":[{"label":"Bi1","element":"Bi","wyckoff":"6c","site_symmetry":"3m","oxidation_state":3.0,"cn":6,"ligands":"Se6","shape":"octahedron","polyhedron":true,"reason":"ok"},{"label":"Se1","element":"Se","wyckoff":"3a","site_symmetry":"-3m","oxidation_state":-2.0,"cn":6,"ligands":"Bi6","shape":"octahedron","polyhedron":true,"reason":"ok"},{"label":"Se2","element":"Se","wyckoff":"6c","site_symmetry":"3m","oxidation_state":-2.0,"cn":3,"ligands":"Bi3","shape":"planar","polyhedron":false,"reason":"only 3 ligand(s): too few to enclose a volume"}],"crystal_chemistry":{"pauling_rule_1_radius_ratio":[{"site":"Bi 6c","radius_ratio":0.5202,"predicted_cn":6,"observed_cn":6,"agrees":true}],"pauling_rule_2_electrostatic_valence":[{"site":"Se 3a","sum_of_electrostatic_bond_strengths":3.0,"anion_charge":2.0,"relative_deviation":0.5,"satisfied":false},{"site"